WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.802
Imagine hearing a phone number in a noisy room.

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:05.906
You keep the digits while letting the background chatter pass.

00:00:05.906 --> 00:00:09.369
Can a sequence model learn which pieces of its input to keep?

00:00:10.019 --> 00:00:14.888
In the Transformer, each new position can compare itself with
earlier positions.

00:00:14.888 --> 00:00:19.187
Across the whole sequence, the number of comparisons grows
quadratically.

00:00:19.187 --> 00:00:21.885
A state space model carries a running summary.

00:00:21.885 --> 00:00:29.366
At each step, it scales the old state, adds a contribution from
the current token, and reads an output from the updated state.

00:00:29.366 --> 00:00:33.166
The memory is the same size after ten tokens or ten thousand.

00:00:33.816 --> 00:00:36.943
Mamba makes three quantities depend on the current token.

00:00:36.943 --> 00:00:43.669
Delta controls how far the dynamics advance. In this decay
example, a small delta preserves more of the old state.

00:00:43.669 --> 00:00:48.027
B controls what the input writes. C controls what the output
reads.

00:00:48.027 --> 00:00:53.696
When filler arrives, the state can barely change. When a useful
token arrives, it can update.

00:00:53.696 --> 00:00:59.354
On the paper's synthetic selective copying task, Mamba scored
ninety-nine point eight percent.

00:01:00.004 --> 00:01:03.955
How can a GPU parallelize an update that needs the preceding
state?

00:01:03.955 --> 00:01:09.532
Each token specifies a transformation: multiply the incoming
state, then add a value.

00:01:09.532 --> 00:01:12.659
Two adjacent transformations can be combined into one.

00:01:12.659 --> 00:01:19.699
Because grouping them differently gives the same result, a
parallel prefix scan can build the transformation up to every
position.

00:01:19.699 --> 00:01:24.346
At fixed state size, the total work grows linearly with the
number of tokens.

00:01:24.346 --> 00:01:29.946
The groups stay in sequence order. Combining a pair means
applying its first update before its second.

00:01:30.596 --> 00:01:37.613
Mamba fuses the conversion to discrete updates, the scan, and
the output projection inside fast on-chip memory.

00:01:37.613 --> 00:01:43.607
It sends the outputs back to main GPU memory and rebuilds the
expanded states during the backward pass.

00:01:43.607 --> 00:01:47.094
This uses the same memory traffic insight as Flash Attention.

00:01:47.094 --> 00:01:55.260
In the authors' benchmark, Mamba reached four to five times the
generation throughput of a similarly sized Transformer, helped
by larger batches.

00:01:55.260 --> 00:02:00.500
Without a key value cache that grows with the prompt, more
sequences fit in the same memory.

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:08.189
Mamba learns what to retain, write, and read, then uses a
hardware-aware scan to compute that memory efficiently.
